# Diagnostic trace for coherence protocol validation
# Run with: python3 moesi_sim.py diagnostic.trace --cores 4 --capacity 8 --verbose
#
# === Pattern A: Silent E->M upgrade and eviction ===
# A cache line obtained via read (Exclusive state) then written
# (silent upgrade to Modified) must preserve dirty data through
# eviction and subsequent reads by other cores.
0 READ 0x0100
0 WRITE 0x0100 0xCAFE
0 WRITE 0x0140 0x1001
0 WRITE 0x0180 0x1002
0 WRITE 0x01C0 0x1003
0 WRITE 0x0200 0x1004
0 WRITE 0x0240 0x1005
0 WRITE 0x0280 0x1006
0 WRITE 0x02C0 0x1007
0 WRITE 0x0300 0x1008
1 READ 0x0100
#
# === Pattern B: E->S sharer tracking ===
# When an Exclusive-state directory entry transitions to Shared
# upon a second reader, all sharing cores must be tracked so that
# future writes correctly invalidate every copy.
2 READ 0x0400
3 READ 0x0400
0 WRITE 0x0400 0xDEAD
2 READ 0x0400
